Subject: [PATCH 70/71] Put the auto-compaction limit back to 80k

`c1b028d1d4` lowered it to 70k on the reasoning that the restored assistant tail raises the
post-compaction floor, so the peak prompt should come down to match. Measured on the `wire` task,
that trade lost:

  Suffice at 70k    27 requests   2 compactions
  upstream at 80k   25 requests   1 compaction

The turn-by-turn dump says where the two extra requests went. Both sides read at the same
granularity - 10 read turns for 23 files here against 11 for 33 there - but the search counts are
15 against 7. Every one of those eight extra searches is the second compaction being paid for:
compaction destroys the tool outputs, so the model re-derives with `rg` what it had already read,
and at 70k it had to do that twice. Suffice reached the limit having read *fewer* files than the
80k side.

A compaction costs a full ~74k summariser request plus the climb back. That is more than the lower
peak is worth on any task that reads its way through a corpus.

